 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Anisotropy:** MipNeRF uses multivariate Gaussians which are anisotropic; this method uses spheres to ensure isotropic pre-filtering, which is required for Tri-Mip encoding [S1].
-*   **Empty Space:** Without an occupancy grid, computation is wasted in empty areas [S1].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** If the ray direction is parallel to an AABB face, the intersection logic must handle division by zero correctly [G].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If $\|\mathbf{d}\|_2 = 0$ or $f^2 > \|\mathbf{d}\|_2^2$, the radius formula becomes undefined; clamp or handle gracefully [G].
